  "title": "Respond to safety outcome (Event Coordinator)",
  "note": "Jira SPM-131 AC1-AC6 and Confluence matrix 36798544 / case pages 36831297, 36896834, 36831315, 36700305, 36798580, 36896852 are authoritative. User clarification (2026-11-01): Pending review is safety-specific metadata keyed to arrangement IDs; request-changes marks only selected venue/technical arrangements, rejection marks all active venue/equipment arrangements, and the Coordinator sees the markers while operational approval statuses stay intact. A Safety Officer response leaves the queue; after edits and resubmission, the event returns to that queue. SPM-135 provides confirmation readiness, feedback resolution and re-request. AC1 adds a durable coordinator notice. Rejection leaves event Planning and does not cancel it or release bookings. AC4 request-changes payloads must identify at least one affected arrangement on every row; legacy reason-only or changes:string[] requests are refused because they cannot implement the selected-only marker contract.",
